@vasild I don't think adding more knobs is the right direction, we already have `-walletbroadcast` which arguably could the a soft default with private broadcast on. Users could over-ride that and retain old behavior. But of course, users may turn the feature on, then turn it back off, rebroadcasting anyways.

>  It is documented that -privatebroadcast does not affect the wallet.

We can change documentation if we change behavior. Only matters if the change is correct/good/etc.

@davidgumberg yeah, I am quite skeptical of the wallet rebroadcast feature, it's built around corner cases and is a massive leak. Would be willing to discuss alternatives in an issue regardless of how this PR goes.

comments.body:
```suggestion
    if (context.args->GetBoolArg("-privatebroadcast", DEFAULT_PRIVATE_BROADCAST)) {
        return;
    }
```

IMO should return here without ever being resubmitted to the mempool since learning a peer's mempool is trivial for an active observer.

